From ed3f840655078aef3c2bb4e6b9a1d26f8e868e64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:41:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ggml-cuda: pipelined long-sequence FlashAttention for
 unmasked attention without GQA packing

The mma FlashAttention kernels without GQA packing (ncols2 == 1, used whenever
there is no mask) load every K/V tile synchronously with an out-of-bounds check,
because the KV length need not be a multiple of the KV tile. For diffusion
transformers (no mask, 10^4 tokens) the kernel then spends most of its time
waiting on global memory.

The long-sequence variant pipelines all full KV tiles with cp.async (the
existing two-stage path) and loads only the final, partial tile synchronously
with the bounds check. Per output element the arithmetic and its order are
unchanged, so results are bit-identical to the stock kernel.

It is used for head sizes 64 and 128 with K == V head size, no mask, no sinks,
no logit softcap and KV length >= 256, on NVIDIA GPUs with cp.async (Ampere and
newer). GGML_CUDA_FA_LONGSEQ=0 restores the stock kernels.

GGML_CUDA_FA_LONGSEQ_NCOLS=128 additionally selects a 128-column tile with 8
warps for Q length >= 1024 (stream-k splits then differ, so results are not
bit-identical); off by default.

test-backend-ops gains unmasked FLASH_ATTN_EXT cases with partial last KV
tiles, several Q tiles and GQA broadcast.
