From e6e78b0ba7477be2b0e6869e19bf86ac89b0381b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 07:36:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ggml-cuda: long-sequence FlashAttention takes the stock
 grid; 128-column tile opt-in only

The stream-k grid is sized from occupancy, and the pipelined variant can have a
different occupancy than the stock kernel (two-stage shared memory), which
moves the stream-k seams and with them the order in which partial results are
combined (measured on L4: relative L2 6e-4 at the op, 36 dB PSNR end to end
over 4 diffusion steps). Size the grid from the stock kernel of the same tile
instead, so the pipelined variant is a bit-identical drop-in on every GPU.

The 128-column tile cannot match the stock seams, so it is no longer a default
on any architecture; GGML_CUDA_FA_LONGSEQ_NCOLS=128 opts in.
---
 src/ggml-cuda/fattn-common.cuh  |  8 +++++--
 src/ggml-cuda/fattn-mma-f16.cuh | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

