-// half the K/V traffic per FLOP). GGML_CUDA_FA_LONGSEQ_NCOLS=64|128 overrides the per-architecture default.
-// Measured at MiniMax-H3 DiT shapes (19108 tokens, 56 heads x 128): 128 is faster on A100 (sm80) and L4 (sm89), neutral on
-// RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (sm120) and B200 (sm100), and slower for head size 64 on A100, so it is only the default there.
+// Q columns per CUDA block of the long-sequence variant for long Q: 64 (the stock tile, default) or 128 (8 warps sharing
+// each K/V tile, half the K/V traffic per FLOP). 128 is opt-in via GGML_CUDA_FA_LONGSEQ_NCOLS=128: it was measured faster at
+// MiniMax-H3 DiT shapes on A100 (sm80, 75 -> 70 ms) and L4 (sm89, 460 -> 365 ms) but splits the work differently from the
+// stock kernel, so its results are not bit-identical.
 static int ggml_cuda_fattn_mma_longseq_ncols(const int cc, const int DKQ) {
     static const int env = [] {
